Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: near-grey system palette (black and white 2.0)

The system palette style is SPRITZ, Android's near-grey style, instead of
TONAL_SPOT, so Settings and SystemUI surfaces are grey rather than tinted
blue. The seed stays Sable Blue (#2E9BD6) for the accent. The first-boot
default in SableFrameworkOverlay uses the same style.
---
 src/com/android/settings/sable/SableAppearancePolicy.java | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/com/android/settings/sable/SableAppearancePolicy.java b/src/com/android/settings/sable/SableAppearancePolicy.java
index 1807ade..73edae4 100644
--- a/src/com/android/settings/sable/SableAppearancePolicy.java
+++ b/src/com/android/settings/sable/SableAppearancePolicy.java
@@ -88,7 +88,7 @@ public final class SableAppearancePolicy {
     public static final String KEY_COLOR_INDEX = "android.theme.customization.color_index";
     public static final String KEY_APPLIED_TIMESTAMP = "_applied_timestamp";
     public static final String COLOR_SOURCE_PRESET = "preset";
-    public static final String THEME_STYLE = "TONAL_SPOT";
+    public static final String THEME_STYLE = "SPRITZ";
 
     private SableAppearancePolicy() {}
 
